/-!
# `Work.MotAS.ASRul.det_submatrix_kleinMAS`

The determinant of the principal `4 × 4` minor of the AS Klein matrix `kleinMAS` is (minus) the
square of the corresponding AS Pfaffian, in characteristic `5`:

  `((kleinMAS a b g y).submatrix k.succAbove k.succAbove).det = - (kleinPAS a b g y k)^2`.

This is the AS analogue of `Work.MotK.TGen.det_submatrix_kleinTwM_eq`, and it is the rank input of
the fibre lemma `Work.MotAS.ASRul.kleinMAS_fibre` (the kernel of `kleinMAS y` is the line spanned by
`kleinPAS y`): `kleinPAS y ≠ 0` gives a coordinate `k` with `kleinPAS y k ≠ 0`, hence an invertible
principal minor.

The identity holds **in characteristic `5` only**: over `ℤ` one has
`det + (kleinPAS k)² = 5 * Z_k`, and the proof below exhibits the explicit cofactor `Z_k` for each
`k` (the AS data of `ASData.lean` are the mod-`5` reductions of the transported split data).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option maxHeartbeats 3200000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

namespace Work.MotAS.ASRul

open Matrix MvPolynomial

